# Troubleshooting Notes

## Camera Preview Window Error

### Symptom

Running:

```bash
rpicam-hello
```

displayed:

```text
Preview window unavailable
```

### Cause

Raspberry Pi was being accessed remotely via SSH from an Android phone.

The `rpicam-hello` application attempts to open a local display window, but no display server was available.

### Resolution

Ignored the warning and used image capture commands instead:

```bash
rpicam-jpeg -o test.jpg
```

### Outcome

Camera functionality verified despite preview warning.

---

## Confirming Camera Functionality

### Initial Uncertainty

The camera appeared to start but there was no visible image output.

### Investigation

Captured a JPEG:

```bash
rpicam-jpeg -o test.jpg
```

Verified file creation:

```bash
ls -lh test.jpg
```

### Resolution

Hosted the file using Python HTTP server:

```bash
python3 -m http.server 8000
```

Viewed image from phone browser:

```text
http://192.168.1.22:8000/test.jpg
```

### Outcome

Confirmed camera hardware and image capture were functioning correctly.

